# Qwen3-235B-A22B (Alibaba, Apache-2.0): the original hybrid release, run in non-thinking mode like our other Qwen3 rows.
# Approved by the user 2026-10-05. Two A100 80GB (tensor parallel): neither 4-bit file fits on one GPU.
# Checked 2026-10-05:
#   - SGLang: Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-GPTQ-Int4 (official, 124.6 GB, float16).
#   - head: lmsys/Qwen3-235B-A22B-EAGLE3 (MIT, SGLang team; hidden 4096, vocabulary 151,936, 40,960 positions).
#     nvidia/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Eagle3 also exists (its own config flags; not used).
#   - Ollama tags moved, as for Qwen3-30B-A3B: qwen3:235b = "Qwen3 235B A22B Thinking 2507" (a different model);
#     qwen3:235b-a22b-q4_K_M = "Qwen3 235B A22B" (the original, 142.4 GB). Read from the GGUF headers.
# Pod: GPUS=2 DISK_GB=500 POD_NAME=sushila-qwen3-235b bash scripts/bench70b/create_pod.sh
MODEL=qwen3-235b-a22b
TARGET=QuixiAI/Qwen3-235B-A22B-AWQ                # AWQ of the original release (Apache-2.0)
PUB_HEAD=lmsys/Qwen3-235B-A22B-EAGLE3
OLLAMA_TAG=qwen3:235b-a22b-q4_K_M
SF_TEMPLATE=qwen
CHAT_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking": false}'
SYSTEM_TURN=0
CTX=4096
TP=2                                             # SGLang and the hidden-state capture split the model over 2 GPUs
# SGLang 0.5.21 hung (50 min) capturing the "breakable" prefill CUDA graph with the EAGLE-3 head over 2 GPUs (TP=2), as
# on Gemma 3. Prompt processing runs without a CUDA graph for every SGLang setup of this model; decoding keeps its graphs.
SGLANG_EXTRA="--cuda-graph-backend-prefill disabled --disable-custom-all-reduce"
# hidden-state capture: the 4-bit weights take 75.4% of each 80 GB GPU at TP=2, so capture needs more than the default 0.75
CAPTURE_MEM=0.88
# 2026-10-05: Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-GPTQ-Int4 gives garbage on SGLang 0.5.21 at TP=2 ("10 10 10...", '"]"]"]') with every
# setting tried (gptq_marlin kernel; custom all-reduce off; float16; CUDA graphs off), while Ollama answers correctly.
# QuixiAI/Qwen3-235B-A22B-AWQ (same original release) answers correctly: use it.

# Pinned: the exact files behind the published results (from precomputed/qwen3-235b-a22b/CHECKSUMS.json). The pipeline downloads
# these revisions, refuses an Ollama file with another sha256, and RETEST=1 uses HEAD_SHA256 from files.sushila.ai.
TARGET_REV=1df91c166baa937f2d571a9cece7a1037c1cc772
PUB_HEAD_REV=d75f968c7d9d19ebdfb1a2fbdd176d61a032da14
OLLAMA_SHA256=aeacdadecbed8a07e42026d1a1d3cd30715bb2994ebe4e4ca4009e1a4abe8d5d
HEAD_SHA256=23834c8c5388f3c75296fb24ce9eafe2e517571d3f31e13978e362d5d01c2549
HEAD_CONFIG_SHA256=1db941ebb1d2ed05ff322c65092a297e421e1268b23d7d7b4bc43bb5702f4c78
